                <pb facs="0613" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2437: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Arica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von
                            Tresckow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-13T11:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Lassiter. Your telegram June 12, 11 a.m. If Edwards comes forward at meeting
                    tomorrow with any suggestion which can possibly be construed as bona fide effort
                    to bring about reasonable adjustment of plebiscitary difficulty without at same
                    time forcing you to take extreme measure represented by your termination
                    resolution, please endeavor to take an adjournment and then cable me.</p>
                <pb facs="0614" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>
                <p>Should he launch any attack upon you, or the Arbitrator, or the United States,
                    you should reply for the Commission and transmit to us immediately what he has
                    said. If he makes public his speech of June 5 or any remarks that he will make
                    tomorrow, then your replies should receive like publicity. Keep us fully and
                    promptly informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
